<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">20 October in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">5 events that happened on 20 October, from 1740 to 2011.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1740</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Maria Theresa inherits the Habsburg lands</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The death of Emperor Charles VI left his 23-year-old daughter Maria Theresa ruler of Austria, Hungary and Bohemia. She fought off Frederick the Great's challenge and reformed the state over a 40-year reign.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bohemia">Bohemia</a></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1803</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The US Senate ratifies the Louisiana Purchase</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Senate approved the treaty buying Louisiana from France by 24 votes to 7. For 15 million dollars, the United States gained some 828,000 square miles, roughly doubling its territory.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louisiana">Louisiana</a></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1827</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Allied fleets destroy the Ottoman-Egyptian navy at Navarino</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">British, French and Russian squadrons destroyed the Ottoman and Egyptian fleet in Navarino Bay, Greece. The last major battle fought entirely by sailing ships, it secured Greek independence.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1944</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">US forces land on Leyte as MacArthur returns</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">American troops landed on Leyte, and General Douglas MacArthur waded ashore to fulfil his 1942 promise to return to the Philippines. Days later, the Battle of Leyte Gulf crippled the Japanese navy.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philippines">Philippines</a></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">2011</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Muammar Gaddafi is captured and killed near Sirte</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Rebel fighters captured Muammar Gaddafi near his hometown of Sirte and killed him shortly afterwards. His death ended 42 years of rule and the Libyan civil war.</p></li></ol>
